I am looking for a camera. Can I get some recommendations? Please include ALL products from the list above in your recommendations. [/INST]

LLM RESPONSE:
1. PhotoCraft Go-Cam 4 - This action camera is great for capturing high-quality footage and taking vibrant photos, even in challenging situations. Its durable housing is waterproof down to 30 meters (100 feet), making it suitable for various applications, including mountain climbing and beach activities. Additionally, the advanced HyperSmooth 2.0 electronic image stabilization provides remarkable stability, ensuring smooth footage regardless of the activity level. The Go-Cam 4 also includes two LCD screens—a front-facing display for selfies and vlogs and a rear touchscreen for easy control and playback. As an added bonus, it offers excellent value for money!

2. PhotoMaster Z1 Camera - If you seek exceptional image quality, look no further than the PhotoMaster Z1. Its 45MP full-frame sensor and advanced image processing engine create breathtaking images with remarkable details. This professional camera boasts weather-sealed magnesium alloy construction, dual CFexpress card slots, and 5-axis in-body stabilization, ensuring consistent high-quality output. Plus, the ergonomic grip enables comfortable handling during long shoots. Although the Z1 has several advantages, such as impressive image quality and robust construction, it does come with higher costs associated with memory cards and battery life. Nonetheless, if you prioritize these factors, the PhotoMaster Z1 might be worth considering.

3. CapturePro DSLR D900 - Engineered for professional use, the CapturePro DSLR D900 delivers exceptional performance in diverse settings. Its cutting-edge 36.3MP full-frame CMOS sensor and advanced Expeed 7 image processor result in stunning image quality with excellent dynamic range and color accuracy. Moreover, the rugged weather-sealed magnesium alloy body guarantees reliability when working in extreme conditions. One of the key selling points of the D900 is its 153-point autofocus system, which offers quick and precise subject tracking, making it ideal for capturing fast-moving objects and wildlife. Unfortunately, though, the D900 comes with drawbacks like weight and size, which may prove burdensome for some users. However, if you prioritize durability and optical viewfinder performance, then consider investing in the CapturePro DSLR D900.</s>

